A||N||9||kornholio||my car is stalling then restarting by it self||||9
Z||000000||kornholio||10-07-1999||07:50 PM||||Just today my car kept stalling everytime I hit a bump in the road and starting right up by itself with out me turning the key. I thought it was just a bad connection, but it wasn't. It did this 4 or five times while driving down the road. Then the car stalled and would not idle at all (I had to keep my foot on the gas to keep it running). 10 minutes later the car would idle in park, but immediately stall after shifting into drive or reverse. I had the car towed to the mechanic's. I went over there an hour later just to check it out. The car started right up, and it doesn't even stall after shifting into drive or reverse. It seemed totally normal, but I left it there anyway. I have no idea what could be wrong. I know that there is coolant leaking from my waterpump, but the engine was not overheating. The temp gauge was cold. Please help! Thanks.||||reg||9
Z||000001||TOM||10-07-1999||08:38 PM||||Dude I think you have gremlins in there. It does sound like a bad connection that is rattling around.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-07-1999||09:49 PM||||did you check the harness connectors by the battery? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||kornholio||10-07-1999||09:52 PM||||Yeah, I checked the wires near the battery. They are all connected nice and tight. I am stumped.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kornholio||10-07-1999||09:56 PM||||I forgot to mention that I got a code 32 EGR system just this morning while driving. I replaced the EGR valve a few months ago. The EGR system has nothing to do with the power going out, does it??||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||10-07-1999||10:41 PM||||Ok, I'll take a wild guess.. Maybe the water pump leak is allowing coolant (when hot) to spray onto the EGR selenoid.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||K9||10-07-1999||11:36 PM||||check the connection detween the coil and dis. cap.(check all wires) Start the car and wiggle the connections between the coil and the dis. cap. DO NOT TOUCH THE SPARK PLUGE WIRE WITH THE CAR RUNNING!||||reg||1
Z||000007||TOM||10-07-1999||11:46 PM||||Hey K9. If you cant touch your spark plugs wires while its running then you need new wires. If they discharge to your hand they will discharge to the manifold and everything else they are near.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shiner||10-08-1999||12:59 AM||||About the spark plug wires, and more specificly, NOT touching them...<P>While doing to timing on my old '84, I did manage to get shocked from the distributor area.  Not a whole lot of fun really.  It makes you jump about ten feet in the air!  That and my arm was a little twitchy.... no bigy. lol.  Of course, I have been fascinated with the interaction between electricity and my body since childhood...  ||||reg||7
Z||000009||kornholio||10-08-1999||05:20 AM||||Well, I guess my car doesn't really start up by itself... It's just that the rpm's drop to 0 and I thought that my car stalled out. In fact it was just the power going out for a split second then coming back on. if the power stays out, then my car stalls.||||reg||1
